ESLint error due reading prefs in effect. We can avoid by using lazy state initializer reading localStorage? But SSR hydration mismatch if localStorage differs. Alternative use useSyncExternalStore for prefs, or initialize defaults and read preferences via event handler only? We want persist. Could use `useState` lazy initializer:
```
const [difficulty, setDifficulty] = useState<Difficulty>(() => typeof window === "undefined" ? "operator" : readPrefs().difficulty)
```
This causes hydration mismatch if stored differs because server renders operator, client first render overclock. React hydration isn't fatal but can mismatch labels. Better avoid: use `useSyncExternalStore` for prefs with stable snapshot? We can create external prefs store with cached snapshot and subscribe to custom event. This is robust and avoids setState-in-effect.

Implement a small external store:
```
let prefsSnapshot: Prefs | null = null;
const PREFS_EVENT = "vantage-signal-sweep-prefs-change";
function getPrefsSnapshot(): Prefs {
 if (!prefsSnapshot) prefsSnapshot = readPrefs();
 return prefsSnapshot;
}
function subscribePrefs(cb) {
 window.addEventListener("storage", cb);
 window.addEventListener(PREFS_EVENT, cb);
 return ...
}
function savePrefs(next) { prefsSnapshot=next; storage; dispatch }
```
But on server `getPrefsSnapshot` would access window. useSyncExternalStore takes `getServerSnapshot` -> DEFAULT_PREFS. Use:
```
const prefs = useSyncExternalStore(subscribePrefs, getPrefsSnapshot, () => DEFAULT_PREFS);
const difficulty = prefs.difficulty;
const muted = prefs.muted;
```
Then no separate states. Actions call `savePrefs({...prefs,...})`. Need stable object reference; cache in module. On hydration React uses server snapshot then getSnapshot; updates. Good.
But module-level prefsSnapshot shared across requests/server? getPrefsSnapshot only called client. Server snapshot constant. Fine.
`getPrefsSnapshot` checks typeof window? Could return default on server too.

`savePrefs(next)`:
```
prefsSnapshot = next;
try localStorage...
window.dispatchEvent(new Event(PREFS_EVENT));
```
`subscribePrefs` add listeners. On storage event from another tab, we need invalidate snapshot so next getSnapshot reads fresh. If prefsSnapshot is cached, storage event won't update. Add listener in subscribe:
```
function onStorage(event) { if (event.key === PREFS_KEY || event.key === null) prefsSnapshot = null; cb(); }
```
But if we register that per subscriber with closure, multiple. Could simpler `getPrefsSnapshot` always parse localStorage, returning a new object -> useSyncExternalStore warning. Cache with checksum raw string:
```
let cachedRaw: string | null = null;
let cachedPrefs: Prefs = DEFAULT_PREFS;
function getPrefsSnapshot() {
 if (typeof window === "undefined") return DEFAULT_PREFS;
 try {
   const raw = window.localStorage.getItem(PREFS_KEY) ?? "";
   if (raw !== cachedRaw) { cachedRaw = raw; cachedPrefs = parse(raw); }
   return cachedPrefs;
 } catch { return DEFAULT_PREFS; }
}
```
This reads localStorage on every render but cheap. Stable object. On any change storage writes raw, next snapshot new object. For same-tab, dispatch custom event to notify. On cross-tab storage event notify. Good. `savePrefs` just writes localStorage + dispatch; no manual cache. If storage unavailable, prefs won't persist but state won't update? Then actions need immediate update. Could fallback module memory. Simpler: allow in-memory snapshot if localStorage fails:
```
let memoryPrefs: Prefs | null = null;
function getPrefsSnapshot() { if (memoryPrefs) return memoryPrefs; ... }
function writePrefs(prefs) { memoryPrefs=prefs; try localStorage...; dispatch; }
```
But when storage available, memoryPrefs set to next and cache persists; cross-tab won't update because memoryPrefs. Hmm.
Alternative: always set memoryPrefs and in storage event set memoryPrefs = null then notify. But module-level storage listener only when subscribed. Could handle getPrefsSnapshot with a `prefsVersion`? Overkill.

Simpler accept no cross-tab preference sync (best score syncs). Use module memory:
```
let prefsCache: Prefs | null = null;
function getPrefsSnapshot() {
 if (prefsCache) return prefsCache;
 if (typeof window === "undefined") return DEFAULT_PREFS;
 prefsCache = readPrefs(); return prefsCache;
}
function writePrefs(next) { prefsCache = next; try localStorage...; dispatch event; }
```
On first client read, loads from storage. Hydration: getServerSnapshot default then getSnapshot returns from storage. Works. Cross-tab storage event triggers callback, but prefsCache still old. We can add a storage listener in subscribe to invalidate cache:
```
function onStorage(event: StorageEvent) {
 if (event.key === PREFS_KEY || event.key === null) {
   prefsCache = null;
   callback();
 }
}
```
So subscribePrefs handles. Good.

But module state during SSR? `prefsCache` remains null on server. Fine.
Potential multiple sessions? only client module.

Same for best: current useSyncExternalStore inline getSnapshot read localStorage returns number stable. Fine.

Need replace `const [difficulty, setDifficulty]` etc. Use:
```
const prefs = useSyncExternalStore(subscribePrefs, getPrefsSnapshot, () => DEFAULT_PREFS);
const { difficulty, muted } = prefs;
```
Then remove effect. `toggleMuted` writePrefs({difficulty, muted: next}) no setMuted.
`selectDifficulty` writePrefs...
`start` unaffected.
`keyboard m` writePrefs...
Need setState for mute removed. `writePrefs` dispatch updates store -> component re-renders. Good.
No useEffect.
`readPrefs` currently try/catch returns default. `getPrefsSnapshot` uses.
`DEFAULT_PREFS` constant frozen maybe.
```
const DEFAULT_PREFS: Prefs = { difficulty:"operator", muted:false };
```
Object stable across server and client; getServerSnapshot returns same. Good.

`subscribePrefs`:
```
function subscribePrefs(callback) {
 function onStorage(event: StorageEvent) {
   if (event.key === PREFS_KEY || event.key === null) { prefsCache = null; callback(); }
 }
 window.addEventListener("storage", onStorage);
 window.addEventListener(PREFS_EVENT, callback);
 return ...
}
```
`PREFS_EVENT` define.
`getPrefsSnapshot`:
```
let prefsCache: Prefs | null = null;
function getPrefsSnapshot(): Prefs {
 if (prefsCache) return prefsCache;
 if (typeof window === "undefined") return DEFAULT_PREFS;
 prefsCache = readPrefs();
 return prefsCache;
}
```
`readPrefs` catches.
`writePrefs`:
```
prefsCache = prefs;
try localStorage.setItem... catch {}
window.dispatchEvent(new Event(PREFS_EVENT));
```
If localStorage throws, re-render still via dispatch, so session behavior persists in memory.
`writeBest` no change.

Fast refresh warnings 2: file exports Route plus component? Existing warning likely only one; now perhaps because `GamePage` plus Route? Warning at 213 and 798? Wait line 798 ControlButton? Let's see. Could ignore warnings, existing had two. No errors.

